During a flash sale, GET /products/sku-123 receives 3,000 requests per second, spread over 8 API instances. Each instance does:

let product = await redis.get(key);
if (!product) {
  product = await db.loadProduct(id);   // ~400 ms under load
  await redis.set(key, product, { EX: 60 });
}

The key expires at 20:00:00. What happens in the next half second?
